"Let $nK_2$ be the disjoint union of $n$ edges, and let a **$k$-super graceful labeling** be a bijective labeling of its vertices and edges by a consecutive integer interval beginning at $k$, with each edge label equal to the sum of the labels of its endpoints. **Consecutive-edge-label conjecture.** Every $k$-super graceful $nK_2$ admits a labeling whose edge-label set is\n\n$$\n[k,k+n-1].\n$$\n\nThe claim concerns normalization of super graceful labelings for matchings; the paper gives examples and no proof or resolution of the general assertion."